& [SelfWorkingDependencyRules]
  + SOP boot identity never implies process launch or workspace mutation authority
  + work planning precedes mutation and mutation precedes verification acceptance or publication
  + a Cantor-authored SOP is an attributable proposal and cannot sign activate or widen its own authority
  + cryptographic review-signature integrity does not prove reviewer competence semantic truth policy governance physical source custody or activation authority
  + provider-free SWA-07 precedes live SWA-08 and neither closes operator-product isolation trust recovery or support

& [DependencyRules]
  + NHC-01 precedes every child or model authority
  + NHC-02 and NHC-03 precede NHC-04
  + NHC-04 through NHC-06 precede any provider-free integration
  + NHC-07 precedes live NHC-08
  + operator-product NHC-09 cannot be inferred from a successful live experiment

& [StopRules]
  + stop on identity collapse implicit model loading hidden launch authority shared-forward-pass claim unbounded attention lost attribution fabricated provider availability or imported independent drafts

